(Houseplant Care Guide) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Watering) Tj T*
(Most houseplants die from too much water, not too little. Push a finger) Tj T*
(two centimetres into the soil: water only when it feels dry at that depth.) Tj T*
(Succulents and cacti need water every two to three weeks in summer and) Tj T*
(almost none in winter. Always use pots with a drainage hole.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Light) Tj T*
(A monstera or a fiddle leaf fig wants bright indirect light near an east) Tj T*
(or west window. Snake plants and ZZ plants tolerate low light corners.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
